{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["And Moshe called Hoshea son of Nun Joshua — he did not call him this now, for he had already been called Joshua earlier. Rather, this is its meaning: 'Hoshea son of Nun,' whom we mentioned above — who was called that in his father's house — he is the same one whom Moshe called [Joshua] when he became his attendant and whom he appointed over his household, for such was their practice, as in: ״ויקרא פרעה שם יוסף צפנת פענח״, and: ויקרא לדניאל די שמיה בלטשצר — according to the name of his god."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:05.718488516Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}